  "$comment": "Copy to models.config.json (or set MODELS_CONFIG_FILE). The browser can only pick models listed here; the Gateway rejects anything else. Model ids are OpenRouter slugs (https://openrouter.ai/models). TTS voices are filled in from OpenRouter automatically when a model lists none (MODELS_DISCOVER_VOICES). Per-model \"params\" (and group-level llm.params) are merged into the OpenRouter chat request body server-side, e.g. reasoning effort or provider routing; they are never sent to the browser. TTS entries may set \"format\" (e.g. \"pcm\" for models that only emit raw PCM; the Gateway wraps it as WAV) and \"sampleRate\". \"voice\" lists audio-native models that hear the user directly and talk (live conversation mode); \"llm\" is the deep brain the voice hands harder work and visuals to. TTS \"emotionTags\": true means the voice performs cues like [laughs]; otherwise they are stripped.",
